# Force LF line endings on files that run inside Linux containers.
#
# Windows users with `core.autocrlf=true` (the default) would otherwise have
# git rewrite these to CRLF on checkout. Linux can't parse a shebang line
# `#!/bin/bash\r\n` — the trailing CR makes the kernel look for an interpreter
# named "/bin/bash\r" and fail with "no such file or directory" (which is
# misleading; the script file itself does exist).
#
# Applies on commit AND on checkout; existing tree should be renormalised with:
#   git add --renormalize .
#   git commit -m "Renormalize line endings per .gitattributes"

*.sh                text eol=lf
Dockerfile          text eol=lf
docker-entrypoint.sh  text eol=lf
*.dockerignore      text eol=lf

# Anything else: let git decide (default behaviour).
